invariant: INV-26
file: aes.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: aes_traffic_key_load keeps the cipher byte the stored schedule
  holds, so zero bytes, a wiped schedule's, would run their AEAD on the
  S-box table, which INV-26 keeps every traffic key away from.
  bin/aes_runtime_test loads zero bytes and reads the cipher byte back.

--- old
#ifdef CH_AES_TWO_CIPHERS
    k->key.instructions = AES_ON_INSTRUCTIONS;
#endif
    aes_traffic_key_cpu(k, cpu);
--- new
    aes_traffic_key_cpu(k, cpu);
